			Arithmetic Operators

Five Arithmetic Operators
	• Addition +
	• Subtraction -
	• Multiplication *
	• Division /
	• Modulus %

Modulus Example
	• often called the remainder operator
	• returns the remainder of a division
		23 % 5 = 3
		11 % 3 = 2

	• to determine an even number
		24 % 2 = 0
		o 0 means an even number
		o 1 means an odd number
	• to determine the day of the week
		(6 + 10) % 7 = 2
		o 6 is Saturday (the seventh day of the week)
		o in 10 days, the day of the week will be Tuesday (day 2)

Integer Division
	• when dividing two integers
		o the result is an integer
		o the fraction is truncated
	• example:
		int num = 5 / 3;
		o num will equal 1
	• to determine time
		int seconds = 100;
		int minutes = seconds / 60;
		int remainingSeconds = seconds % 60;

Order of Precedence
	• the order that expressions are evaluated
	• use BEDMAS
		o Brackets
		o Exponents

	 Multiplication and Division
		 from left to right
	o Addition and Subtraction
		 from left to right
	• us parenthesis to avoid confusion

	• examples
		int num = 10 + 5 / 5;
			 num is 11
		int num = (10 + 5) / 5;
			 num is 3
		double digit = 10 + 5 / 5;
			 digit is 11.0 
